  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nHigh pressure centered over New England slides south through\nSunday with a dry cold front crossing late Monday.Return flow\naround the high will allow high temperatures to trend upwards\ntomorrow into Monday with areas south of the mountains seeing\nmid to upper 60s.\n\nThe front crossing late Monday may bring some light showers near\nthe Canadian Border. Otherwise the front crosses with little\nfanfare by Tuesday morning. Another cool Canadian High pressure\nbuilds in behind the front Tuesday that will allow for another \ncold night Tuesday night with lows in the teens and 20s.\nTemperatures moderate through the end of the week as the high\nslowly migrates east of the area.",
